Repair the complete source below and return one corrected source file. `chooseVisible` treats items sharing a non-null `group` as one atomic candidate; ungrouped items are separate candidates. Reject duplicate item IDs, non-finite or negative widths, and non-finite priorities with `RangeError`. Reject a non-finite or negative capacity likewise. Candidate width is the sum of its items, priority is the maximum item priority, and first position is its earliest input index. Consider candidates by descending priority, then ascending first position. Select a candidate if its entire width fits in remaining capacity; otherwise skip it and continue. Return selected IDs in original input order and hidden IDs likewise. Empty input is valid. Do not mutate or alias inputs.

